speechtext:
The minister said a
moment ago that if we were hard enough up we could get along without this. I wonder if we are not at that stage right now. The minister says the United States can afford to send twenty-three delegates over, but the United States can afford to be extravagant;
I do not think Canada can. Now the minister tells us that we can get out of this by notifying the other countries that we are not going to take part in it, and I would suggest that he take that step. I grant that he is not responsible for this organization; it has been bequeathed to him, but why not take another*step in the right direction and on the grounds of economy notify the other contracting parties to this agreement that as far as Canada is concerned we intend to withdraw for this year at least.
